# Naming Conventions

Always use fully qualified, descriptive names for variables, parameters, and functions. Do not abbreviate.

```typescript
// BAD
const sol = bifrost.solution.getSolution();
const dir = bifrost.files.getContainingDirectory(uri);
const cmd = bifrost.commands.getClickHandler();
const ctx = event.context;
const destPath = joinPaths(target, name);
const doc = editors.getEditorDocument();

// GOOD
const currentSolution = bifrost.solution.getSolution();
const containingDirectory = bifrost.files.getContainingDirectory(uri);
const clickHandler = bifrost.commands.getClickHandler();
const context = event.context;
const destinationPath = joinPaths(target, name);
const editorDocument = editors.getEditorDocument();
```

Exceptions: Single-character names are acceptable only in sort comparators (`a`, `b`) and loop indices (`i`, `j`).
